<title>MEXICO: BANCO DE MEXICO TO DRAIN 4.835 BLN PESOS.</title>
<headline>BANCO DE MEXICO TO DRAIN 4.835 BLN PESOS.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-08-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Banco de Mexico sought to drain 4.835 billion pesos from the secondary market on Tuesday through a combination of three direct sales of paper and eight repurchase agreements, dealers said.</p>
<p>The Cetes sales were offered or assigned as follows:</p>
<p>    AMOUNT     TERM	 AVERAGE RATE</p>
<p>    150 million    352 days   20.78 pct</p>
<p>    150 million    177 days</p>
<p>    150 million     86 days</p>
<p>The amounts and maturities of the repurchase agreements were offered as follows:</p>
<p>    500 million     48 days</p>
<p>    500 million     45 days</p>
<p>    500 million     44 days</p>
<p>    800 million     41 days</p>
<p>    500 million     16 days</p>
<p>    800 million	9 days</p>
<p>    650 million	3 days</p>
<p>    135 million	1 day</p>
<p>*Amounts in pesos</p>
<p>(( --Mexico City newsroom +525 728-9559))</p>
</text>
